  {
    
    "name": "Section 16",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-612312029583115227 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/bg1v1z-zg/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_STATIC&editorId=612312029432120283&sectionId=612312029583115227)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"gg8xnZX25D__text","label":"gg8xnZX25D__text","default":"Frequently Asked Questions"},{"type":"html","id":"ggDDh0Z1Hrj_childItem_0","label":"ggDDh0Z1Hrj_childItem_0","default":"<p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\"><strong>How long until I see results?</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggDDh0Z1Hrj_childItem_1","label":"ggDDh0Z1Hrj_childItem_1","default":"<p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\"><strong>Can I take Peak Form with my thyroid medication?</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggDDh0Z1Hrj_childItem_2","label":"ggDDh0Z1Hrj_childItem_2","default":"<p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\">Why liquid instead of pills?</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggaJVVSC6EO_text","label":"ggaJVVSC6EO_text","default":"<p>Most women notice early shifts like <strong>less puffiness, steadier energy, and clearer thinking within 1–2 weeks</strong>. More visible “body response” changes (like <strong>weight finally moving / less bloating / more consistent days</strong>) typically build over <strong>4–12 weeks</strong> with daily use.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gglymLOhXEZ_text","label":"gglymLOhXEZ_text","default":"<p>Yes — Peak Form is designed to <strong>work alongside thyroid medication</strong>, not replace it. Many customers take Peak Form at a <strong>different time of day</strong> than their prescription (common choice), but routines vary. If you have questions, share the ingredient list with your provider.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggLEFgZo8Ll_text","label":"ggLEFgZo8Ll_text","default":"<p>Because consistency and absorption matter. Many women with thyroid issues also deal with sluggish digestion, so capsules can be hit-or-miss. Peak Form’s liquid drops are quick to take, easier to stay consistent with, and designed to absorb fast — so your body can actually use the nutrients instead of letting them pass through.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjwDs21BNw_childItem_0","label":"ggjwDs21BNw_childItem_0","default":"<p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\"><strong>How do I take it?</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjwDs21BNw_childItem_1","label":"ggjwDs21BNw_childItem_1","default":"<p><span style=\"font-size:15px;\"><strong>Is it safe for Hashimoto’s or autoimmune thyroid conditions?</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjwDs21BNw_childItem_2","label":"ggjwDs21BNw_childItem_2","default":"<p>What if I’ve tried other thyroid supplements that didn’t work?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggykBu0DtC4_text","label":"ggykBu0DtC4_text","default":"<p>Take <strong>1 full dropper (1ml) once daily</strong>. You can take it <strong>directly under your tongue</strong> for fast absorption, or <strong>mix it into a small glass of water</strong>—whatever you’ll do consistently.<br><br><span style=\"font-size:15px;\"><i>Hold for 10–15 seconds before swallowing for quicker absorption. (Optional line)</i></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggP2CJ_K7UJ_text","label":"ggP2CJ_K7UJ_text","default":"<p>Many customers with Hashimoto’s use Peak Form, and the formula is designed with thyroid-supportive dosing in mind. That said, autoimmune thyroid conditions can be individual - especially around iodine sensitivity and medication dosing - so the safest approach is to <strong>share the ingredient list with your healthcare provider</strong> before starting. If you have <strong>hyperthyroidism/Graves</strong> or are under active medical management, consult your provider first.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggFgKFT-cKl_text","label":"ggFgKFT-cKl_text","default":"<p>You’re not alone - most thyroid supplements are <strong>underdosed</strong>, missing key cofactors, or built like generic multivitamins. Peak Form is different because it’s designed around the <i>activation side</i> of thyroid function (the step many women stay stuck on), uses <strong>clinically relevant doses</strong>, and comes in <strong>fast-absorbing liquid drops</strong> so it’s easier to take consistently. That’s also why we back it with a <strong>60-day risk-free guarantee</strong>.</p>"}],
